{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>If his master gives him a wife.</b> Rashi's comment: a Canaanite maidservant. From here [we learn] that the master has authority to give him a Canaanite maidservant to beget children from her. Since the master is obligated to provide food for his wife and children, the authority is in the master's hand to give him a Canaanite maidservant to beget slaves from her. One may object: is it not written in the perasha Ki Tetze, לא יהיה קדש, and Onkelos translates: 'A man of Israel shall not take a maidservant as a wife'? And there Rashi commented that he too becomes a קדש through her, since all his acts of intercourse are acts of harlotry, as kiddushin do not take effect with her. <b>Gives him a wife.</b> The wording proves that she is a Canaanite, for she was in his [the master's] hand to give to him; if she were a Hebrew [maidservant], he would have no power to give her in marriage without her consent — only his minor daughter, concerning whom it is written את בתי נתתי." "<b>The woman and her children.</b> The children follow her in every respect, and so it says, עבדך בן אמתך."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:12.873049968Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}